.vscode/**
src/**
tsconfig.json
data/**
docs/**
*.vsix
.gitignore
package-lock.json
node_modules/**
PUBLISHING.md
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/*.js.map
# Patterns meant to match at any depth need an explicit **/ prefix here.
# .vscodeignore is not gitignore: a bare `*.md` only matches top-level entries,
# which silently shipped every docs/*.md file into an earlier release.
**/*.md
!README.md
.claude/**
*.zip
private_backup/**
tests/**
.github/**
.bench_workload.py

# python/ is deliberately NOT excluded.
#
# The instrumentation ships as readable .py files. It used to be base64-encoded
# into extension.js, written to globalStorage at runtime and executed from
# there — which is the textbook packer pattern regardless of intent, and it hid
# the one part of this extension a security reviewer most needs to read.
# Shipping plain source is both the correct posture for an AGPL project and the
# honest answer to a scanner flag.
